  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For a simple harmonic motion in a mass spring system shown, the surface is frictionless. When the mass of the block is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, the angular frequency is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. When the mass block is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> the angular frequency is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/861dba8a-dda9-4a16-b006-5dccd6d5693e-21218936-f367-42ee-a85b-3926958fb97f-image.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 79px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
